  automatically in generated HTML: before ; : ! ? and %, after an opening «,
  between groups of 3 digits in a number the source already spaces out
  (e.g. "170 000"), between a number and million(s)/milliard(s)/dollar(s)/$,
  and after × or ≈ before a number. It only ever upgrades a space the
  source already has to a non-breaking one — it never inserts spacing or
  digit grouping that wasn't there, and a non-breaking space already in
  the source is always left exactly as written.

  Three article-level <!-- lwp:meta --> fields turn part or all of this
